          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "నేరం — nēraṁ — \"a crime; an offence\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "దొంగతనం పెద్ద నేరం. doṅgatanaṁ pedda nēraṁ. Theft is a serious crime."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: నేరాలు, nērālu."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "నేరం (nēraṁ) చేయు, to commit a crime."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "నేరం (nēraṁ) is native Dravidian: DEDR 3775 lists Telugu nēramu, \"fault, offence, crime\", with Tamil nēram, \"guilt, fault\"."
            }
          ]
        },
